WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.431
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B one.

2
00:00:05.731 --> 00:00:09.304
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.604 --> 00:00:15.820
Unit twenty-three: Reflexive Pronouns. Today you will show that the subject and the object are the same.

4
00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:18.807
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.767 --> 00:00:23.359
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.217 --> 00:00:25.206
Myself.

7
00:00:26.217 --> 00:00:28.692
Myself means reflexive form of I.

8
00:00:29.283 --> 00:00:30.668
I taught myself.

9
00:00:31.283 --> 00:00:33.785
Your turn. Say: Myself.

10
00:00:36.633 --> 00:00:37.634
Myself.

11
00:00:38.383 --> 00:00:39.210
Yourself.

12
00:00:40.217 --> 00:00:42.576
Yourself means reflexive form of you.

13
00:00:43.183 --> 00:00:44.475
Enjoy yourself.

14
00:00:45.083 --> 00:00:48.026
Your turn. Say: Yourself.

15
00:00:50.867 --> 00:00:51.891
Yourself.

16
00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:53.616
Himself.

17
00:00:54.617 --> 00:00:56.709
Himself means reflexive form of he.

18
00:00:57.317 --> 00:00:58.515
He hurt himself.

19
00:00:59.117 --> 00:01:01.583
Your turn. Say: Himself.

20
00:01:04.433 --> 00:01:05.551
Himself.

21
00:01:06.317 --> 00:01:07.225
Herself.

22
00:01:08.217 --> 00:01:10.495
Herself means reflexive form of she.

23
00:01:11.083 --> 00:01:12.468
She made it herself.

24
00:01:13.083 --> 00:01:15.933
Your turn. Say: Herself.

25
00:01:18.767 --> 00:01:19.675
Herself.

26
00:01:20.417 --> 00:01:21.499
Ourselves.

27
00:01:22.483 --> 00:01:24.553
Ourselves means reflexive form of we.

28
00:01:25.150 --> 00:01:26.650
We enjoyed ourselves.

29
00:01:27.250 --> 00:01:30.030
Your turn. Say: Ourselves.

30
00:01:32.867 --> 00:01:34.158
Ourselves.

31
00:01:34.917 --> 00:01:36.266
Themselves.

32
00:01:37.250 --> 00:01:39.691
Themselves means reflexive form of they.

33
00:01:40.283 --> 00:01:41.691
They did it themselves.

34
00:01:42.283 --> 00:01:44.936
Your turn. Say: Themselves.

35
00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:49.091
Themselves.

36
00:01:49.850 --> 00:01:50.967
By myself.

37
00:01:51.983 --> 00:01:54.145
By myself means alone, without help.

38
00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:56.297
I live by myself.

39
00:01:56.883 --> 00:01:59.768
Your turn. Say: By myself.

40
00:02:02.633 --> 00:02:03.751
By myself.

41
00:02:04.517 --> 00:02:05.378
Enjoy.

42
00:02:06.383 --> 00:02:08.499
Enjoy means to like doing something.

43
00:02:09.083 --> 00:02:10.410
Enjoy yourself!

44
00:02:11.017 --> 00:02:13.506
Your turn. Say: Enjoy.

45
00:02:16.367 --> 00:02:17.484
Enjoy.

46
00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:21.962
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:22.817 --> 00:02:25.315
Visal, what have you taught yourself to do?

48
00:02:26.417 --> 00:02:34.061
I have taught myself to play the guitar. We use a reflexive pronoun when the subject and the object are the same person.

49
00:02:35.150 --> 00:02:36.790
Which pronouns do we have?

50
00:02:37.883 --> 00:02:48.145
Myself, yourself, himself, herself, itself, ourselves, yourselves, themselves. Note the plural: selves. He cut himself. We enjoyed ourselves.

51
00:02:49.250 --> 00:02:50.948
What does by myself mean?

52
00:02:52.050 --> 00:03:07.534
It means alone or without help: I did it by myself. But some verbs do not need a reflexive in English: I wash, I dress, I relax. We do not say I feel myself tired.

53
00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:10.502
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:11.350 --> 00:03:15.393
Grammar focus: Reflexive pronouns: myself, yourself….

55
00:03:15.693 --> 00:03:16.938
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:17.650 --> 00:03:19.859
I taught myself to play the guitar.

57
00:03:20.750 --> 00:03:22.065
He hurt himself.

58
00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:24.508
We enjoyed ourselves.

59
00:03:25.467 --> 00:03:33.193
Use myself, yourself, himself, herself, itself, ourselves, yourselves, themselves when the subject and object are the same. By myself = alone.

60
00:03:33.950 --> 00:03:37.252
Be careful! Don't say: He cut him yesterday.

61
00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:41.850
Say: He cut himself yesterday.

62
00:03:42.150 --> 00:03:43.360
Use himself.

63
00:03:44.167 --> 00:03:47.051
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:47.867 --> 00:03:49.088
Doing It Yourself.

65
00:03:49.388 --> 00:03:51.388
I taught myself to play the guitar.

66
00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:54.527
My brother cut himself while cooking.

67
00:03:55.533 --> 00:03:57.521
We enjoyed ourselves at the festival.

68
00:03:58.533 --> 00:04:00.359
She made this dress by herself.

69
00:04:01.367 --> 00:04:03.076
They built the house themselves.

70
00:04:04.167 --> 00:04:08.052
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:08.917 --> 00:04:10.545
She hurt blank yesterday.

72
00:04:10.845 --> 00:04:13.825
A, her. B, herself. C, she.

73
00:04:17.367 --> 00:04:19.111
The answer is B: herself.

74
00:04:20.250 --> 00:04:22.226
We enjoyed blank at the party.

75
00:04:22.526 --> 00:04:25.982
A, us. B, ourselves. C, ours.

76
00:04:29.533 --> 00:04:31.394
The answer is B: ourselves.

77
00:04:32.550 --> 00:04:34.448
I did it blank. (alone)

78
00:04:34.748 --> 00:04:38.761
A, by myself. B, myselves. C, me self.

79
00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:44.218
The answer is A: by myself.

80
00:04:45.383 --> 00:04:47.267
Which plural form is correct?

81
00:04:47.567 --> 00:04:51.313
A, themself. B, themselves. C, theirselves.

82
00:04:54.867 --> 00:04:57.168
The answer is B: themselves.

83
00:04:58.317 --> 00:05:01.071
According to the reading, what did the brother cut?

84
00:05:01.371 --> 00:05:04.630
A, himself. B, the table. C, the fruit.

85
00:05:08.167 --> 00:05:09.876
The answer is A: himself.

86
00:05:11.067 --> 00:05:14.114
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:14.950 --> 00:05:16.891
What have you taught yourself to do?

88
00:05:25.683 --> 00:05:27.137
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:27.437 --> 00:05:38.463
I have taught myself to cook Khmer noodles. I watched videos and practised by myself. Now my family enjoys the food, and I feel proud of myself.

90
00:05:38.763 --> 00:05:40.228
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:41.117 --> 00:05:46.869
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and reflexive pronouns: myself, yourself….

92
00:05:47.169 --> 00:05:51.760
Today's value is independence. Learn to do things by yourself, step by step.

93
00:05:52.060 --> 00:05:55.049
See you in Unit twenty-four. Goodbye!

94
00:05:55.349 --> 00:05:57.920
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

